\version "2.24.0"
% SECOND THEME (theme F2), bars 51-66, E flat minor, Poco meno mosso: the trumpet's soft melody owed since movement I
% (cyclic-notes 'Owed' item 1): trumpet 1 alone, undoubled, no timpani and no other brass in its register (Adler PDF 264, 267);
% the octave doubling (flute 1) is saved for its climax at 61-62 (Adler PDF 279-281). E flat (III) is a key neither earlier movement uses.
% Accompaniment: upper strings pizz. off the beat, cellos and basses pizz. on the beat, clarinets and bassoons sustained pp.
% The theme is heard first in minor and then in major (67), the reverse of movement I's second theme (cyclic-notes).

% c032 (harmony; A&S Unit 17, PDF 283, Ex. 17-24: the Phrygian IV6-V): 57 Cl 2 E flat3 on beat 3 (was A flat3: A flat-B flat under the solo's E flat-F, parallel 5ths into V at 58).
% c046 (Adler PDF 292, 321: slurred notes are one breath; with no rest between the 4-bar slurs the player must cut a note): breath marks after 54, 58, 62 (and 174, 178, 182 in recS with the cor anglais)
% c048 (expression; A&S Unit 3, PDF 54-55: the accented dissonance carries the stress, its resolution is lighter): 62 the diminuendo starts on beat 2, after the peak B flat 5, and covers the falling group (was on beat 4 only); same at 182 in recS
sOneTptOne = { bes'2.(\p^\markup \italic "dolce cantabile" ges'4 | f'4 es'4 ges'4 bes'4 | f''2 es''4 des''4 | ces''2 bes'2) \breathe | aes'2.( ces''4 | bes'4 aes'4 ges'4 f'4 | ges'2 es'2 | f'1) \breathe | bes'2.( ges'4 | f'4 es'4 ges'4 bes'4\< | es''2. f''4 | bes''4\mf aes''4\> ges''4 f''4) \breathe | es''2.(\p des''4 | ces''4 bes'4 aes'4 ges'4 | f'2 d'2 | es'1) | }
% c041 (melody; Adler ch. 7, PDF 185-186: the flute's top fourth is "a bit shrill", hard to play softly, best approached by scale): 61-63 Fl 1 doubles the soft trumpet at the unison (F5-B flat5) instead of the octave (leap F6-B flat6 at p-mf above a p solo).
sOneFluteOne = { R1*10 | r2 r4 \once \override Staff.Hairpin.springs-and-rods = #ly:spanner::set-spacing-rods \once \override Staff.Hairpin.minimum-length = #7 f''4(\p\< | bes''4\mf aes''4\> ges''4 f''4) | es''2.(\p des''4) | R1*3 | }
